---
// How to print, cut and fold a `MiniZine`, for the top of any page that
// carries one. Screen only: the sheet has no room for it, and by the time it
// is printed the reader has read it.
---

<div class="no-print">
  <p>
    Eight pages from one sheet of US Letter, printed on one side and folded
    into a mini zine — one cut, no staples. Print at actual size (100%),
    landscape, with no margins.
  </p>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      Fold the sheet in half, then in half again, then once more, so it is
      creased into eight panels.
    </li>
    <li>
      Fold it in half side to side. From the folded edge, cut along the middle
      crease as far as the next crease — the solid line.
    </li>
    <li>
      Unfold it, then fold it in half the long way with the printing outside.
      Push the two ends towards each other so the cut opens into a diamond, and
      keep pushing until it folds flat.
    </li>
    <li>Wrap the pages round so the front cover is on top.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<style>
  p,
  .steps {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .steps {
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
